2	 * chainprobe.c -- read-only dlmod probe for snmpd.
3	 *
4	 * Answers one question with a runtime readout instead of inference: for an OID
5	 * that in-master registers, does net-snmp keep the other registrations for the
6	 * same range on subtree->children, and in what order?
7	 *
8	 * dump_registry() cannot answer it (it walks ->next only), and the children
9	 * merge path in agent_registry.c:845-935 has no DEBUGMSG, so there is no way
10	 * to read this from outside the process.
11	 *
12	 * Strictly read-only: it walks the registry and writes a text file. It never
13	 * registers, unregisters, or mutates anything except its own trigger OID.
14	 *
15	 * Trigger:  snmpget .1.3.6.1.4.1.8691.9999.1.0   -> writes /tmp/chain.txt,
16	 *                                                   returns the chain count.
